<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>test case of <span id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PTA-GRPO</span></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="591.87" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 591.87" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,591.87) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E2EAF9;" fill="#E2EAF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 13.19 L 0 578.67 C 0 585.96 5.91 591.87 13.19 591.87 L 536.81 591.87 C 544.09 591.87 550 585.96 550 578.67 L 550 13.19 C 550 5.91 544.09 0 536.81 0 L 13.19 0 C 5.91 0 0 5.91 0 13.19 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF6EA;" fill="#FFF6EA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 13.19 L 1.38 534.95 L 548.62 534.95 L 548.62 13.19 C 548.62 6.67 543.33 1.38 536.81 1.38 L 13.19 1.38 C 6.67 1.38 1.38 6.67 1.38 13.19 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 543.73)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.85em;--ltx-fo-height:3.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.82)" width="454.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.85em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">Generated Samples in Real Test cases of <span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PTA-GRPO</span> (Sample 1)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 17.08)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.78em;--ltx-fo-height:36.54em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="509.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 505.63)" width="522.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.78em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Determine the interval of convergence for the series</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\frac{x}{2}+\frac{2!x^{2}}{3^{2}}+\frac{3!x^{3}}{4^{3}}+\ldots" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\frac{x}{2}+\frac{2!x^{2}}{3^{2}}+\frac{3!x^{3}}{4^{3}}+\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="103.72" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.75 103.72" width="522.75"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,103.72) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD3E0;" fill="#CCD3E0" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.7 L 0 95.02 C 0 99.82 3.9 103.72 8.7 103.72 L 514.05 103.72 C 518.86 103.72 522.75 99.82 522.75 95.02 L 522.75 8.7 C 522.75 3.9 518.86 0 514.05 0 L 8.7 0 C 3.9 0 0 3.9 0 8.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 8.7 L 0.83 81.89 L 521.92 81.89 L 521.92 8.7 C 521.92 4.36 518.4 0.83 514.05 0.83 L 8.7 0.83 C 4.36 0.83 0.83 4.36 0.83 8.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 89.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.38em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;plan&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 12.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.09em;--ltx-fo-height:4.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="62.11" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 59.42)" width="499.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.09em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">1. Identify the general term of the series.
2. Apply the Ratio Test to find the radius of convergence.
3. Check the endpoints of the interval separately to determine convergence or divergence there.
4. State the final interval of convergence.</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="320.35" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.75 320.35" width="522.75"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,320.35) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CFDED7;" fill="#CFDED7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.7 L 0 311.64 C 0 316.45 3.9 320.35 8.7 320.35 L 514.05 320.35 C 518.86 320.35 522.75 316.45 522.75 311.64 L 522.75 8.7 C 522.75 3.9 518.86 0 514.05 0 L 8.7 0 C 3.9 0 0 3.9 0 8.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 8.7 L 0.83 298.51 L 521.92 298.51 L 521.92 8.7 C 521.92 4.36 518.4 0.83 514.05 0.83 L 8.7 0.83 C 4.36 0.83 0.83 4.36 0.83 8.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 305.97)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.38em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;think&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 13.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.09em;--ltx-fo-height:19.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="278.74" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 275.28)" width="499.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.09em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">We start by writing down the general term of the series. The pattern is clear: the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th term looks like</span>
<span id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n!}{(n+1)^{n}}x^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n!}{(n+1)^{n}}x^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p">To test for convergence, the Ratio Test is natural. Taking the ratio <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n+1}/a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n+1}/a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, most factors cancel, and it reduces to</span>
<span id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|\left(\frac{n+1}{n+2}\right)^{n+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|\left(\frac{n+1}{n+2}\right)^{n+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the power term tends to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. So the limit is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|/e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|/e</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Ratio Test, convergence requires <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|/e&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|/e&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|&lt;e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|&lt;e</annotation></semantics></math>. That gives us the radius of convergence <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=e</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p">Now check the endpoints. At <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=e</annotation></semantics></math>, the terms are <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n!}{(n+1)^{n}}e^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n!}{(n+1)^{n}}e^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Stirling’s formula shows that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n!\sim(n/e)^{n}\sqrt{2\pi n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n!\sim(n/e)^{n}\sqrt{2\pi n}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the terms behave like <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}</annotation></semantics></math> times a constant. They don’t go to zero, so the series diverges. At <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-e</annotation></semantics></math>, the alternating sign doesn’t help because the size of the terms again grows like <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. They still don’t go to zero, so the series diverges there as well.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the series converges only strictly inside the interval, and the interval of convergence is</span>
<span id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-e,e)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-e,e).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{(-e,\,e)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{(-e,\,e)}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="488.55" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 488.55" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,488.55) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E2EAF9;" fill="#E2EAF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 13.19 L 0 475.36 C 0 482.64 5.91 488.55 13.19 488.55 L 536.81 488.55 C 544.09 488.55 550 482.64 550 475.36 L 550 13.19 C 550 5.91 544.09 0 536.81 0 L 13.19 0 C 5.91 0 0 5.91 0 13.19 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF6EA;" fill="#FFF6EA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 13.19 L 1.38 431.63 L 548.62 431.63 L 548.62 13.19 C 548.62 6.67 543.33 1.38 536.81 1.38 L 13.19 1.38 C 6.67 1.38 1.38 6.67 1.38 13.19 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 440.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.85em;--ltx-fo-height:3.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.82)" width="454.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.85em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">Generated Samples in Real Test cases of <span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PTA-GRPO</span> (Sample 2)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 13.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.78em;--ltx-fo-height:29.33em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="405.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 405.78)" width="522.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.78em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> What is the least possible value of the sum <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x-1|+|x-1.5|+|x-2|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x-1|+|x-1.5|+|x-2|</annotation></semantics></math>?</span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="120.32" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.75 120.32" width="522.75"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,120.32) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD3E0;" fill="#CCD3E0" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.7 L 0 111.62 C 0 116.43 3.9 120.32 8.7 120.32 L 514.05 120.32 C 518.86 120.32 522.75 116.43 522.75 111.62 L 522.75 8.7 C 522.75 3.9 518.86 0 514.05 0 L 8.7 0 C 3.9 0 0 3.9 0 8.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 8.7 L 0.83 98.49 L 521.92 98.49 L 521.92 8.7 C 521.92 4.36 518.4 0.83 514.05 0.83 L 8.7 0.83 C 4.36 0.83 0.83 4.36 0.83 8.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 105.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.38em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;plan&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 12.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.09em;--ltx-fo-height:5.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="78.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.03)" width="499.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.09em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">1. Recognize that this is a minimization problem involving sums of absolute values.
2. Recall that for a sum of absolute values of linear functions, the minimum occurs at a median of the points.
3. Identify the points: 1, 1.5, and 2.
4. Determine the median of these three points.
5. Calculate the sum at the median point to find the minimum value.</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="219.8" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.75 219.8" width="522.75"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,219.8) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CFDED7;" fill="#CFDED7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.7 L 0 211.09 C 0 215.9 3.9 219.8 8.7 219.8 L 514.05 219.8 C 518.86 219.8 522.75 215.9 522.75 211.09 L 522.75 8.7 C 522.75 3.9 518.86 0 514.05 0 L 8.7 0 C 3.9 0 0 3.9 0 8.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 8.7 L 0.83 197.96 L 521.92 197.96 L 521.92 8.7 C 521.92 4.36 518.4 0.83 514.05 0.83 L 8.7 0.83 C 4.36 0.83 0.83 4.36 0.83 8.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 205.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.38em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;think&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 12.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.09em;--ltx-fo-height:12.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="178.19" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 175.5)" width="499.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.09em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">We want to minimize</span>
<span id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=|x-1|+|x-1.5|+|x-2|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=|x-1|+|x-1.5|+|x-2|.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p">General fact: For <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x-a_{1}|+\cdots+|x-a_{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x-a_{1}|+\cdots+|x-a_{n}|</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimum occurs when <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is the median of the <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p">Here, the three points are <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,1.5,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,1.5,2</annotation></semantics></math>. Ordered: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;1.5&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;1.5&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math>.
So the median is <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p">Evaluate at <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
<span id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|1.5-1|+|1.5-1.5|+|1.5-2|=0.5+0+0.5=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|1.5-1|+|1.5-1.5|+|1.5-2|=0.5+0+0.5=1.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p">Check at neighbors:</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p">* At <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0+0.5+1=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0+0.5+1=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>.
* At <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+0.5+0=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+0.5+0=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>.
* At <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1.25</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25+0.25+0.75=1.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25+0.25+0.75=1.25</annotation></semantics></math>.
* At <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1.75</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.75+0.25+0.25=1.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.75</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.75+0.25+0.25=1.25</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p">All larger than 1.
Thus, the minimum occurs uniquely at <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>, with value <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="560.89" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 560.89" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,560.89) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E2EAF9;" fill="#E2EAF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 13.19 L 0 547.69 C 0 554.98 5.91 560.89 13.19 560.89 L 536.81 560.89 C 544.09 560.89 550 554.98 550 547.69 L 550 13.19 C 550 5.91 544.09 0 536.81 0 L 13.19 0 C 5.91 0 0 5.91 0 13.19 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF6EA;" fill="#FFF6EA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 13.19 L 1.38 503.97 L 548.62 503.97 L 548.62 13.19 C 548.62 6.67 543.33 1.38 536.81 1.38 L 13.19 1.38 C 6.67 1.38 1.38 6.67 1.38 13.19 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 512.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.85em;--ltx-fo-height:3.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.82)" width="454.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.85em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">Generated Samples in Real Test cases of <span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PTA-GRPO</span> (Sample 3)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 17.08)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.78em;--ltx-fo-height:34.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="478.11" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 474.65)" width="522.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.78em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Find the range of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> for which the stability condition <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ξ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> holds, given that</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}=1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})\,s^{4},\quad s=\sin\left(\tfrac{\omega}{2}\right)\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ξ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}=1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})\,s^{4},\quad s=\sin\left(\tfrac{\omega}{2}\right)\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="121.86" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.75 121.86" width="522.75"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,121.86) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD3E0;" fill="#CCD3E0" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.7 L 0 113.16 C 0 117.97 3.9 121.86 8.7 121.86 L 514.05 121.86 C 518.86 121.86 522.75 117.97 522.75 113.16 L 522.75 8.7 C 522.75 3.9 518.86 0 514.05 0 L 8.7 0 C 3.9 0 0 3.9 0 8.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 8.7 L 0.83 100.03 L 521.92 100.03 L 521.92 8.7 C 521.92 4.36 518.4 0.83 514.05 0.83 L 8.7 0.83 C 4.36 0.83 0.83 4.36 0.83 8.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 107.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.38em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;plan&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 13.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.09em;--ltx-fo-height:5.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="80.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.8)" width="499.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.09em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">1. Understand the stability condition: <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
2. Substitute the given expression for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
3. The stability condition <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
4. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, ensure it is non-negative (<math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>) to avoid complex values.
5. Analyze the sign of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{2}(1-p^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{2}(1-p^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
6. Determine the condition on <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
7. Conclude the range of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="270.53" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.75 270.53" width="522.75"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,270.53) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CFDED7;" fill="#CFDED7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.7 L 0 261.83 C 0 266.64 3.9 270.53 8.7 270.53 L 514.05 270.53 C 518.86 270.53 522.75 266.64 522.75 261.83 L 522.75 8.7 C 522.75 3.9 518.86 0 514.05 0 L 8.7 0 C 3.9 0 0 3.9 0 8.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 8.7 L 0.83 248.7 L 521.92 248.7 L 521.92 8.7 C 521.92 4.36 518.4 0.83 514.05 0.83 L 8.7 0.83 C 4.36 0.83 0.83 4.36 0.83 8.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 256.16)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.38em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;think&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.69 13.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.09em;--ltx-fo-height:16.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="228.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 225.47)" width="499.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.09em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">We have</span>
<span id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}=1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4},\quad s\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}=1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4},\quad s\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p">For stability, we need <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
That means</span>
<span id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p">This simplifies to</span>
<span id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}\leq 0\quad\Rightarrow\quad p^{2}(1-p^{2})\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}\leq 0\quad\Rightarrow\quad p^{2}(1-p^{2})\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, this requires <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p^{2}\geq 0\implies p^{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p^{2}\geq 0\implies p^{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we must ensure <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the term <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4p^{2}(1-p^{2})s^{4}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}=1-\text{(nonnegative)}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mtext>(nonnegative)</mtext></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}=1-\text{(nonnegative)}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This guarantees both realness and the upper bound condition.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p|&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p|&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p^{2}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p^{2}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{2}(1-p^{2})&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{2}(1-p^{2})&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case the subtracted term becomes negative, effectively making <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi|^{2}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi|^{2}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, which breaks stability.</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p">Hence the stability condition holds exactly when</span>
<span id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[-1,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[-1,1].</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A1.SS2.p3.pic1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{[-1,1]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{[-1,1]}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="327.33" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 327.33" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,327.33) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E2EAF9;" fill="#E2EAF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.98 L 0 318.35 C 0 323.31 4.02 327.33 8.98 327.33 L 541.02 327.33 C 545.98 327.33 550 323.31 550 318.35 L 550 8.98 C 550 4.02 545.98 0 541.02 0 L 8.98 0 C 4.02 0 0 4.02 0 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FEFFFE;" fill="#FEFFFE" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 8.98 L 1.11 288.49 L 548.89 288.49 L 548.89 8.98 C 548.89 4.63 545.37 1.11 541.02 1.11 L 8.98 1.11 C 4.63 1.11 1.11 4.63 1.11 8.98 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 296.22)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.54em;--ltx-fo-height:1.88em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.06)" width="450.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.54em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#367DBD;">PTA-GRPO<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> prompt</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 16.11 16.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.64em;--ltx-fo-height:18.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="262.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 259.45)" width="493.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.64em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{{content | trim }}
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Begin by outlining a high-level plan wrapped in &lt;plan&gt;&lt;/plan&gt; tags.
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- This plan should capture only the major phases, strategic choices, and conditional branches.
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Avoid low-level steps, calculations, or detailed reasoning here.
Next, reason step by step within &lt;think&gt;&lt;/think&gt;.
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- During reasoning, critically evaluate the initial plan. If you find any errors, inconsistencies, or improvements needed, revise your plan mentally and continue reasoning based on the revised plan.
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Explicitly state if you are revising the plan and describe the changes.
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- This is your detailed chain-of-thought: work through assumptions, intermediate steps, and logical derivations until the solution is reached.
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Finally, provide the final answer enclosed within
</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,XGJveGVke30=" download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">\</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">boxed</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{}</span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) is a state-of-the-art Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR) algorithm that simplifies Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite> by removing the need for a value model to estimate the baseline advantage, and has demonstrated remarkable success in enhancing the reasoning abilities of LLM.
Formally, let <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of questions, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the current policy model, and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> represent a collection of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> candidate responses sampled for a question <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in Q</annotation></semantics></math>. We also define <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{ref}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{ref}}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a fixed reference model. The training objective of GRPO is expressed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{q\sim Q,\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{q\sim Q,\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathfrak{o}_{i}|}\min\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)}A_{i},\,\text{clip}\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\right)A_{i}\right)-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\text{ref}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mi>min</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext>clip</mtext><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathfrak{o}_{i}|}\min\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)}A_{i},\,\text{clip}\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\mathfrak{o}_{i}^{t}|q)},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\right)A_{i}\right)-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\text{ref}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> controls the clipping range and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> weights the KL regularization term.
The normalized advantage <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> assigned to each response <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{o}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{o}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed from group-based rewards:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=\frac{r_{i}-\mu}{\sigma},\quad\text{with }\mu=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}r_{j},\quad\sigma=\sqrt{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^{N}(r_{j}-\mu)^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=\frac{r_{i}-\mu}{\sigma},\quad\text{with }\mu=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}r_{j},\quad\sigma=\sqrt{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^{N}(r_{j}-\mu)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{1},r_{2},\dots,r_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{1},r_{2},\dots,r_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are the scalar rewards associated with the response group <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In GRPO, each response <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{o}\in\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{o}\in\{\mathfrak{o}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a CoT <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> together with its final answer. As noted in Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Reasoning in Large Language Models ‣ 2 Preliminaries and related work ‣ Plan Then Action: High-Level Planning Guidance Reinforcement Learning for LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, token-level MDPs lack global planning and often yield redundant steps, while GRPO rewards <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{o}</annotation></semantics></math> focus only on final answer correctness, overlooking reasoning quality and enabling reward hacking through superficial or verbose CoTs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Theoretical proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following the framework of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qian et al., 2025</a>)</cite> ,for a fixed <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,t)</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional error rate is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{e}(q,t)=1-\max_{y^{\prime}}\Pr(y=y^{\prime}\mid q,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{e}(q,t)=1-\max_{y^{\prime}}\Pr(y=y^{\prime}\mid q,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the binary distribution <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p,1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p,1-p)</annotation></semantics></math>, it is known that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(p,1-p)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H_{b}(p)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(p,1-p)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H_{b}(p),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{b}(p)=-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{b}(p)=-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary entropy.
This can be generalized to the <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-class case.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability distribution,
and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}=\max_{i}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}=\max_{i}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p_{\max}\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p_{\max}\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof by induction.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Base case <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> This is exactly the binary inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Induction step.</em><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Suppose the inequality holds for <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math> classes.
Consider an <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-class distribution with maximum element <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1-p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1-p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Merge the last two categories into one, obtaining an <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-class distribution <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the grouping property of Shannon entropy,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m-2},p_{m-1},p_{m})=H(\tilde{\bm{p}})+(p_{m-1}+p_{m})H_{b}\!\left(\tfrac{p_{m-1}}{p_{m-1}+p_{m}}\right)\geq H(\tilde{\bm{p}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m-2},p_{m-1},p_{m})=H(\tilde{\bm{p}})+(p_{m-1}+p_{m})H_{b}\!\left(\tfrac{p_{m-1}}{p_{m-1}+p_{m}}\right)\geq H(\tilde{\bm{p}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the induction hypothesis,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1-p_{1}\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(\tilde{\bm{p}})\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1-p_{1}\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(\tilde{\bm{p}})\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the lemma holds for all <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the conditional distribution <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(y\mid q,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(y\mid q,t)</annotation></semantics></math>, the lemma implies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{e}(q,t)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(y\mid q,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{e}(q,t)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(y\mid q,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,t)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{error}}=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}[p_{e}(q,t)]\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(y\mid q,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>error</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{error}}=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}[p_{e}(q,t)]\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(y\mid q,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the chain rule,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(\hat{y};y\mid q,t)=H(y\mid q,t)-H(y\mid\hat{y},q,t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\hat{y};y\mid q,t)=H(y\mid q,t)-H(y\mid\hat{y},q,t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(y\mid q,t)\geq H(y\mid\hat{y},q,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(y\mid q,t)\geq H(y\mid\hat{y},q,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Also,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(y\mid q,t)=H(y)-I(y;q,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(y\mid q,t)=H(y)-I(y;q,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{error}}\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(y\mid q,t)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\bigl[H(y)-I(y;\hat{y}\mid q,t)\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>error</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{error}}\leq\tfrac{1}{2}H(y\mid q,t)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\bigl[H(y)-I(y;\hat{y}\mid q,t)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The theorem is proved.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Experimental parameter setup</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted all experiments on eight H200 GPUs. In the supervised fine-tuning (SFT) stage, we trained Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct for 3 epochs. In the reinforcement learning (RL) stage, we adopted the GRPO algorithm, with a global batch size of 128 and a micro batch size of 4 per GPU. During rollout, the model generated 12 samples per step, including 3 analytic plans, each corresponding to 3 Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning trajectories. For generation, we set temperature = 1.0 and top-p = 1.0, while for validation we used temperature = 0.6, top-p = 0.95, and n = 4. The number of RL training steps was configured as follows: LLaMA3.2-3B and Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct were trained for 350 steps, Qwen3-8B for 150 steps, and Qwen3-14B for 50 steps, with other hyperparameters kept the same across models. In addition, the learning rate (<span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr</span>) was set to <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, the weight decay (<span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight_decay</span>) was <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\times 10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\times 10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimizer was <span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adamw</span> (choices: <span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adamw</span> or <span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adamw_bf16</span>), the learning<span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>rate warmup ratio (<span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr_warmup_ratio</span>) was 0. For all Qwen3-8b, max token is 4.5k and for Qwen2.5-7B-Instrct , the max token is 3.5K.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
